Installation
============

Requirements (Linux)
--------------------
* NVIDIA GPU with a CUDA driver
* CUDA Toolkit 11 or newer (provides nvcc)
* GNU make, bash, and wget or curl (only to download the dataset)
No other libraries are needed: PGM/PNG reading and writing is built in.

Steps
-----
1. Clone the repository:
     git clone <this repository URL>
     cd <repository folder>
2. Download the dataset (about 10 MB):
     bash data/download_data.sh
   If the machine has no internet access, download
   https://kdd.ics.uci.edu/databases/faces/faces.tar.gz yourself, copy it
   into data/ and run the script again.
3. Build:
     make build
4. Run:
     ./run.sh

Windows users: use WSL2 with the CUDA toolkit for WSL, then follow the
Linux steps.
